---
/**
 * The living background, rendered once by BaseLayout on every page: a fixed, full-viewport layer
 * behind all content (z-index −1, no pointer events, hidden from assistive technology).
 *
 * - Always: the paper grain, drawn above the canvas and below the content (::after).
 * - After first paint, where hardware WebGL is usable: the receding halftone sheet of arch glyphs
 *   and the floating 3D logo plates (src/scripts/living-background/), faded in over the paper. It
 *   is cleared to the paper colour (dark paper in the dark theme), so it never shifts anything
 *   and the page looks the same until it arrives.
 * - Theme switch: the canvas is hidden (`is-switching`), swaps inks and paper, and fades back in
 *   (`is-theme-fade` keeps that fade short). The hiding is a cut, not a fade: theme.ts sets
 *   `html.theme-switching` during the switch, which turns transitions off (global.css).
 *
 * The layer is 100lvh tall, so mobile toolbars showing or hiding never resize the canvas. The
 * paper itself is <html>'s background and <body> stays transparent (global.css), so this layer
 * paints between the two.
 */
---

<div class="living-bg" data-living-bg aria-hidden="true"></div>

<script>
  import { initLivingBackground } from '~/scripts/living-background';

  initLivingBackground();
</script>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .living-bg {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      right: 0;
      left: 0;
      z-index: -1;
      height: 100vh;
      height: 100lvh;
      pointer-events: none;
      contain: strict;
    }
    .living-bg :global(.living-bg-canvas) {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      opacity: 0;
      transition: opacity 900ms var(--ease-out);
    }
    .living-bg :global(.living-bg-canvas.is-live) {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    .living-bg :global(.living-bg-canvas.is-live.is-theme-fade) {
      transition-duration: 180ms;
    }
    .living-bg :global(.living-bg-canvas.is-live.is-switching) {
      opacity: 0;
    }
    /* The paper grain (it used to sit on <body>): above the sheet, below the content. */
    .living-bg::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      background-image: var(--grain);
      background-size: 160px 160px;
    }

    @media print {
      .living-bg {
        display: none;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
